# JCM online numerical linking: the jcm-strat AL7h model run live as the meteorology, tomas_jax.fast microphysics, RRTMGP radiation
#
# As jcm_numerical (T63 Gaussian 96x192 grid, the CESM climatology regridded onto
# it, tomas_jax.fast, RRTMGP + Mie), but U/V/OMEGA/T come from jcm-strat
# INTEGRATING beside the aerosol model (MET_SRC=jcm_online) instead of from the
# AL7h70 chain's stored output, with every term of the AL7h configuration active:
# Jucker relaxation + the AL7h T_e correction, QBO nudging, ERA5 nudging of
# u/v/T below 400 hPa, Hines and Lott-Miller drag, the sponge. It is built from
# the chain's own resolved Hydra config and started from the chain's 1 January
# checkpoint. Still one-way: the circulation never sees the aerosol.
#
# Provenance: the 1-year run jcm_online_1yr_inj6_30NS (2026-11-19; same scenario
# as the 2-year JCM run: 6 Tg SO2/yr at 55 hPa, 30N/30S mirrored, lon 180) was
# made with these knob values, this jcm-strat commit (and its jax-gcm
# submodule) and the same tomas-jax / jax-rrtmgp pins, and with the perf
# switches and ADV_SL_RHONORM off, which now default on (that run's values:
# ADV_SL_RHONORM=0 RAD_FAST=0 MICRO_WRAP_DEVICE=0 MAM4_BIN_DEVICE=0 ADV_SL_DEVICE_RESAMPLE=0 CKPT_ASYNC=0).
# The default-on switches were validated (48 h) on cesm_numerical and
# jcm_numerical only, NOT on this linking. Here RAD_FAST=auto resolves on and
# adds ~2 GB of device memory on the GPU the live jcm-strat server shares; if
# that card runs short, or for the tested configuration, set all six to 0 as
# above.
#
# NOT BIT-REPRODUCIBLE, AND IT CANNOT BE. jcm-strat on GPU is not deterministic
# run to run: two identical stock runs from the same checkpoint differ by
# 2.8 m/s in u after 6 h. A rerun of this preset therefore does not reproduce
# that run bit for bit, and this linking is validated STATISTICALLY, never
# bitwise: scripts/validation/validate_jcm_online.py compares band zonal means
# against the stored chain and its year-to-year spread (MANIFEST.md).
#
# GPU memory: the JCM server shares the card with the aerosol model. It keeps
# the year's ERA5 nudging target (~29 GiB) on the HOST and hands each 6-hour
# step a 4-sample slice; on the device it holds a few GiB.
#
# Model slots. jcm-strat is the code the JCM server imports (jcm_strat, and jcm
# from its external/jax-gcm submodule: git submodule update --init --recursive
# models/jcm-strat).
#@submodule tomas-jax  models/tomas-jax  787c991e499342df2dc59c96470bd5f167537868
#@submodule jax-rrtmgp models/jax-rrtmgp 99d2d7174d2e6967c9c45e8f4bae22a4994d1c18 patch=patches/jax-rrtmgp-zenith.patch
#@submodule jcm-strat  models/jcm-strat  f3c20703bcc664dfdbbcd8fad694e915b54696e6

# Meteorology: jcm-strat AL7h run live in a subprocess (src/met/jcm_server.py),
# 6-hourly, on the JCM grid. JCM_DIR (the chain whose checkpoints, template and
# grid it starts from) and JCM_TEMPLATE are left at coupling.py's defaults:
#   /data/JCM_stripped/jcm-strat/runs/p31/p31_AL7h70
#   .../p31_AL7h70_19960101/.hydra/config.yaml
# JCM_TE_CORRECTION is left at its default, the slot's tracked AL7h.nc.
MET_SRC=jcm_online
# Everything else from the CESM climatology regridded onto the JCM grid; Q from
# it too (MET_Q=bc, the default: jcm-strat is dry).
BC_SRC=clim
CLIM_FILE=inputs/bc_clim/bc_clim_jcm.npz
INIT_BIN=so4
ADV_VPOS=1

# MACHINE PATHS (this machine's; not part of any checkout). A submodule checkout
# holds jcm-strat's code but not its virtualenv or its data caches. On another
# machine, point these at your own: a Python 3.11 venv with jcm-strat's
# dependencies (JAX 0.10; models/jcm-strat/scripts/bootstrap_env.sh builds one), its
# cache directory (era5/ = regridded ERA5 nudging windows, fetched on first use;
# huggingface/ = jcm boundary files) and a scratch directory (JAX compile cache).
JCM_PY=/data/JCM_stripped/jcm-strat/.venv/bin/python
JCM_CACHE=/data/JCM_stripped/jcm-strat/cache
JCM_SCRATCH=/data/JCM_stripped/jcm-strat/scratch
